cat > /tmp/SPEC_ADDENDUM.md <<'EOF'
# SPEC ADDENDUM — UnicodeEncodeError message form (VERIFIED against the reference)

The original spec described only the SINGULAR form. CPython emits TWO forms depending on the length of the
FIRST CONTIGUOUS RUN of unencodable (lone-surrogate) characters:

* run length == 1:
  `'utf-8' codec can't encode character '\udcff' in position 0: surrogates not allowed`
  (word "character", singular; includes the Python repr of the single char, lowercase \udcXX)

* run length  > 1:
  `'utf-8' codec can't encode characters in position 0-2: surrogates not allowed`
  (word "characters", plural; NO character repr; range is `start-(end-1)`, i.e. inclusive of the last char)

Only the FIRST run is reported. Positions are PYTHON CODE POINT indices (an astral char counts as 1).

## Verified evidence (passphrase built with printf octal escapes)
| bytes                    | reported                                   |
|--------------------------|--------------------------------------------|
| `a \xff b`               | character '\udcff' in position 1            |
| `\xff a \xff`            | character '\udcff' in position 0  (first run only) |
| `\xff\xff\xff`           | characters in position 0-2                  |
| `x \xff\xff y`           | characters in position 1-2                  |
| emoji + `\xff\xff`       | characters in position 1-2  (emoji = 1 cp)  |
| emoji emoji + `\xff`     | character '\udcff' in position 2            |
| `\xc0\x80` overlong      | characters in position 0-1                  |
| `\xc1\xbf` overlong      | characters in position 0-1                  |
| `\xe0\x80\x80` overlong  | characters in position 0-2                  |
| `\xe0\x9f\xbf` overlong  | characters in position 0-2                  |
| `\xf0\x80\x80\x80`       | characters in position 0-3                  |
| `\xf0\x8f\xbf\xbf`       | characters in position 0-3                  |
| `\xed\xa0\x80` surrogate | characters in position 0-2                  |
| `\xed\xa0\x80\xed\xb0\x80` | characters in position 0-5                |
| `\xf5\x80\x80\x80`       | characters in position 0-3                  |
| `\xf4\x90\x80\x80`       | characters in position 0-3                  |
| `\xc3` truncated         | character '\udcc3' in position 0            |
| `\xc3 A` truncated+ascii | character '\udcc3' in position 0            |
| `\xe4\xb8` truncated     | characters in position 0-1                  |
| `\xe4\xb8 -` trunc+ascii | characters in position 0-1                  |
| `\xf0\x9f\x98` truncated | characters in position 0-2                  |
| `\xf0\x9f\x98 A`         | characters in position 0-2                  |
| `\xc3\xa9\x80`           | character '\udc80' in position 1            |

=> CONFIRMS: the strict UTF-8 decoder rejects **each byte of an invalid sequence individually**, emitting one
U+DC00+byte per rejected byte, and resumes at the byte right after the rejected one.

## Sequences that are VALID and must decode/encode normally (rc=0)
`\xe0\xa0\x80` (U+0800) -> c97787e9bf4e9bbb8a9c2e705ff105347d375e7d
